    "id": "art_triad-augmented-has-no-root",
    "slug": "triad-augmented-has-no-root",
    "title": "One Shape, Three Names",
    "summary": "An augmented triad stacks three equal gaps, so rotating it gives the same shape back — one grip is three chords at once, and the shape underneath has no root of its own.",
    "tags": ["triads", "chords", "fretboard"],
    "readingTimeMin": 3,
    "publishedAt": "2026-08-14"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Rotate an augmented triad and you get the same triad back. That isn't true of any other quality in this pathway, and it means one grip can be three different chords, depending only on which note you call the root."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The reason is arithmetic. Root to third is "
        },
        {
          "text": "4",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " semitones. Third to fifth is "
        },
        {
          "text": "4",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " more. And the fifth back up to the root, wrapping around the octave, is "
        },
        {
          "text": "4",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " again — three equal gaps. Rotating the notes changes nothing about the structure, and rotating the notes is exactly what an inversion does."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Here is the whole lesson in one grip. "
        },
        {
          "text": "x x x 1 1 0",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " on strings 1-2-3 sounds "
        },
        {
          "text": "G#3",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "text": "C4",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " "
        },
        {
          "text": "E4",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " — the same three frets, "
        },
        {
          "text": "spelled",
          "link": {
            "kind": "footnote",
            "id": "fn-augmented-spelling"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " three different ways."
        }
      ]
    },
