    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Move the same shape four frets up and "
        },
        {
          "text": "x x x 5 5 4",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " gives back the same three note names again — now reading as "
        },
        {
          "text": "Caug",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " root position, "
        },
        {
          "text": "Eaug",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " second inversion, "
        },
        {
          "text": "G#aug",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " first inversion."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "On strings 1-2-3 the three inversions sit exactly four frets apart, every time — the bass note at fret 1, then fret 5, then fret 9, and the cycle starting over at fret 13."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "live",
      "component": "triad-ladder",
      "props": {
        "root": "C",
        "quality": "augmented",
        "strings": "1-2-3",
        "caption": "C augmented's three inversions on strings 1-2-3 — four bands, evenly spaced, one shape repeating. Silent, same as every ladder."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The diminished ladder on this same set drew something different — "
        },
        {
          "text": "three bands, unevenly spaced, three different shapes",
          "link": {
            "kind": "article",
            "slug": "triad-diminished-across-the-sets"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ". The numbers say why: augmented is "
        },
        {
          "text": "4 + 4 + 4",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": "; diminished is "
        },
        {
          "text": "3 + 3 + 6",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "tone": "warning",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A diminished chord is often described as symmetrical, sliding in minor thirds. That's true of the four-note diminished seventh — out of scope here — and false of the three-note triad, which is why the two ladders look nothing alike."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Only "
        },
        {
          "text": "four",
          "marks": ["bold"]
        },
        {
          "text": " different augmented triads exist at all: "
        },
        {
          "text": "C",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
