          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": "/"
        },
        {
          "text": "B",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": ". Twelve chord names, four actual sounds. Diminished doesn't share that: there are twelve different diminished triads, one for every root."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The shape has no root of its own — context supplies one. Whichever note is in the bass, or whichever chord the music just came from, is the one the ear hears as the root. That's also why the chord sounds unsettled on its own: with nothing around it, there's no note for the ear to land on. It's the "
        },
        {
          "text": "G",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " underneath a "
        },
        {
          "text": "G+",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " that makes the shape a "
        },
        {
          "text": "G",
          "marks": ["code"]
        },
        {
          "text": " chord — "
        },
        {
          "text": "the same shape, met resolving into C",
          "link": {
            "kind": "article",
            "slug": "triad-the-sharp-fifth"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All four qualities turn out to live under one hand, root never moving — "
        },
        {
          "text": "two fingers' worth of difference away from each other",
          "link": {
            "kind": "article",
            "slug": "triad-all-four-in-one-place"
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "."
        }
      ]
